<urn:atm:triage:finding/FTQ-001-AN15>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "FTQ-001-AN15" ;
  triage:title "timeout_and_failure_remain_best_effort races a fixed 10ms sleep against the async timeout-drop path on loaded Windows runners" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr root-caused a Test(windows-latest) FAILED on PR #880 (feature/an15-adversarial-fuzzing, run 31819546649, job 94829518897) to workflow_telemetry::tests::timeout_and_failure_remain_best_effort, panicked at crates/atm-runtime/src/workflow_telemetry.rs:405:9, assertion left==right failed (left: 0, right: 1). The test configures emit_timeout: Duration::from_millis(1), calls try_emit once, then sleeps a fixed Duration::from_millis(10) before asserting diagnostics().dropped_timeout == 1. On a loaded/slow Windows CI runner the background async task that increments dropped_timeout after the 1ms configured timeout can lose the race against the fixed 10ms sleep, observing 0 instead of 1. Confirmed unrelated to the AN.15 fix under review: this test is in atm-runtime (workflow_telemetry.rs), a different crate from the boundaries-lint fix's atm-template-sc-compose (commit f661a8876, 2-string-literal rename only). Test(macos-latest) and Test(ubuntu-latest) passed on the same run; re-running Test(windows-latest) alone succeeded. Remediation: replace the fixed 10ms sleep with a bounded poll/retry loop (or otherwise await the drop-counter reaching 1 with a generous timeout) instead of a single fixed sleep racing the timeout path. Status corrected open -> deferred by quality-mgr (2026-08-14): intentional-defer rationale (flaky-test root cause fully understood and unrelated to the reviewed fix; matches this record's own reasoning) means it should not have been left open. Status corrected deferred -> open by team-lead/user direction (2026-08-14): flaky tests are not acceptable deferred debt; this flake already caused a real delay (blocked the AN15-SPRINTDOC-STATUS-DRAFT doc-only PR). Real fix dispatched to arch-ctm: replace the fixed 10ms sleep with a bounded poll/retry on the dropped_timeout counter." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-an" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "flaky-test-qa" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "closed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-14T16:50:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AN15 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-14T16:36:54Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:resolutionNotes "Closed 2026-08-14 by quality-mgr: independently verified fix b875b0170c5646e7530a562376a7e8c8826ed3a9 on integrate/phase-an. Both racing fixed-sleep assertions (dropped_timeout and dropped_failure) replaced with a bounded 1s-timeout/2ms-poll wait_for_diagnostic_count() helper with a clear panic diagnostic on timeout, removing the fixed-10ms-sleep-vs-async-drop race entirely. Re-ran `cargo test -p atm-runtime workflow_telemetry::tests --release`: 9/9 pass, including timeout_and_failure_remain_best_effort. Not taken from arch-ctm's self-report." ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/FTQ-001-AN15/AN15-OCC-001> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "4" .

